1
00:01:32,750 --> 00:01:35,020
[Forging Justice]

2
00:01:35,350 --> 00:01:37,680
[Episode 20]

3
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:48,870
Mei.

4
00:01:49,590 --> 00:01:50,920
Qian Xingliang is here.

5
00:01:56,430 --> 00:01:57,560
Will you go meet him?

6
00:02:00,250 --> 00:02:03,490
[Meeting Room 1]

7
00:02:12,910 --> 00:02:14,170
Please... have a seat.

8
00:02:14,750 --> 00:02:16,150
I'm fine squatting.

9
00:02:16,680 --> 00:02:17,650
No, please sit.

10
00:02:17,680 --> 00:02:18,840
We'll talk after you're seated.

11
00:02:18,840 --> 00:02:19,660
Just sit down.

12
00:02:19,680 --> 00:02:20,140
Come on.

13
00:02:25,960 --> 00:02:26,680
Mr. Qian,

14
00:02:27,430 --> 00:02:30,030
I am truly sorry about
what happened years ago.

15
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:31,870
But at that time,

16
00:02:31,870 --> 00:02:33,600
we didn't have a better choice.

17
00:02:33,800 --> 00:02:35,150
After all, investigative capabilities

18
00:02:35,150 --> 00:02:36,280
and the general understanding

19
00:02:36,280 --> 00:02:38,740
back then were vastly different
from today.

20
00:02:39,310 --> 00:02:39,910
That said,

21
00:02:40,360 --> 00:02:41,290
on all accounts,

22
00:02:41,750 --> 00:02:42,840
you still suffered

23
00:02:42,840 --> 00:02:43,970
a great deal of harm.

24
00:02:44,800 --> 00:02:45,910
On my own behalf,

25
00:02:46,710 --> 00:02:48,310
I'd like to apologize to you.

26
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:49,800
It's okay. It's nothing.

27
00:02:50,750 --> 00:02:51,280
Nothing.

28
00:02:51,280 --> 00:02:52,120
Judges, if this is

29
00:02:52,120 --> 00:02:53,380
the attitude you take,

30
00:02:53,750 --> 00:02:55,750
our discussion will be smooth then.

31
00:02:57,980 --> 00:02:58,630
Please sit.

32
00:02:58,630 --> 00:02:59,520
Yes, be seated.

33
00:03:00,310 --> 00:03:01,550
My client

34
00:03:01,570 --> 00:03:03,640
was kept behind bars for a total

35
00:03:03,710 --> 00:03:05,520
of 2,941 days.

36
00:03:06,280 --> 00:03:07,410
During this period,

37
00:03:07,690 --> 00:03:08,750
his home was smashed

38
00:03:08,750 --> 00:03:10,870
by Yu Sanhua's family multiple times.

39
00:03:10,870 --> 00:03:12,070
Right? And his mother

40
00:03:12,210 --> 00:03:13,240
passed away out of grief

41
00:03:13,240 --> 00:03:15,240
and indignation caused by all this.

42
00:03:16,070 --> 00:03:18,200
Who do you think should be responsible

43
00:03:18,240 --> 00:03:19,100
for his losses?

44
00:03:22,030 --> 00:03:23,290
You're suggesting...

45
00:03:24,630 --> 00:03:25,490
I, as Mr. Qian's

46
00:03:26,120 --> 00:03:26,980
representive,

47
00:03:27,430 --> 00:03:29,890
will formally file for state compensation.

48
00:03:43,710 --> 00:03:44,360
Mr. Tan,

49
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:46,770
the State Compensation Law
has just been enacted.

50
00:03:46,770 --> 00:03:47,770
None of us are sure

51
00:03:47,800 --> 00:03:49,329
about its implementation.

52
00:03:49,910 --> 00:03:51,240
Could you please offer

53
00:03:51,520 --> 00:03:52,450
more specifics?

54
00:03:52,750 --> 00:03:54,590
For example, you demand one million here.

55
00:03:54,590 --> 00:03:56,320
-On what ground?
-One million?

56
00:03:56,710 --> 00:03:58,170
That's too much. Too much.

57
00:03:58,380 --> 00:03:59,780
Did I say you could speak?

58
00:04:04,150 --> 00:04:04,470
Tan Xin,

59
00:04:04,470 --> 00:04:05,630
how can you treat him like that?

60
00:04:05,630 --> 00:04:06,830
How do I treat him now?

61
00:04:07,100 --> 00:04:08,240
Don't you remember how you defended him

62
00:04:08,240 --> 00:04:08,840
years ago?

63
00:04:08,860 --> 00:04:09,820
How do you have the nerve

64
00:04:09,820 --> 00:04:10,820
to shut him up now?

65
00:04:11,320 --> 00:04:12,750
No matter how I defended him back then,

66
00:04:12,750 --> 00:04:14,150
you would've sentenced him
to death anyway,

67
00:04:14,150 --> 00:04:14,680
right?

68
00:04:16,310 --> 00:04:17,630
Even if Yuan Yifang had represented him,

69
00:04:17,630 --> 00:04:19,760
would there have been any difference?

70
00:04:19,950 --> 00:04:20,880
I'm warning you,

71
00:04:22,160 --> 00:04:23,120
take our demands

72
00:04:23,120 --> 00:04:23,800
seriously.

73
00:04:24,310 --> 00:04:24,970
Otherwise,

74
00:04:25,160 --> 00:04:26,820
we will raise funds publicly.

75
00:04:27,160 --> 00:04:27,630
Let's see who will be

76
00:04:27,630 --> 00:04:29,090
a national disgrace then.

77
00:04:33,430 --> 00:04:33,960
Let's go.

78
00:04:36,360 --> 00:04:37,560
Thank you, officers.

79
00:04:37,950 --> 00:04:39,550
Wait, why did you thank them?

80
00:04:39,750 --> 00:04:42,750
Would you have been imprisoned
if it weren't for them?

81
00:04:42,870 --> 00:04:43,400
Let's go.

82
00:04:55,120 --> 00:04:56,780
I shouldn't have apologized.

83
00:04:56,870 --> 00:04:57,830
That lawyer has seized on

84
00:04:57,830 --> 00:04:58,830
some words I said.

85
00:04:58,950 --> 00:05:01,080
He'll definitely use them against us.

86
00:05:01,430 --> 00:05:03,270
Whoever does wrong should apologize.

87
00:05:03,270 --> 00:05:04,200
It's only right.

88
00:05:05,800 --> 00:05:06,830
We can't stop

89
00:05:06,830 --> 00:05:07,960
a lightning strike,

90
00:05:08,110 --> 00:05:09,720
but we shouldn't run toward it.

91
00:05:09,720 --> 00:05:10,240
Mei,

92
00:05:10,950 --> 00:05:12,270
Qian Xingliang spent 8 years in prison.

93
00:05:12,270 --> 00:05:13,040
His life is ruined.

94
00:05:13,040 --> 00:05:13,940
Did you not see that?

95
00:05:13,940 --> 00:05:14,940
I did see that.

96
00:05:15,480 --> 00:05:17,160
But what does it have to do with us?

97
00:05:17,160 --> 00:05:18,890
The decision wasn't made by us.

98
00:05:20,800 --> 00:05:22,200
Think whatever you want.

99
00:05:23,310 --> 00:05:24,000
But I can never bring myself

100
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:26,000
to say "it has nothing to do with me."

101
00:05:32,810 --> 00:05:34,690
Justice Blooming in a Corner—

102
00:05:34,720 --> 00:05:35,770
a record of Binjiang Intermediate Court's

103
00:05:35,770 --> 00:05:38,630
Judge Xia Yingjie
clearing a wrongful conviction.

104
00:05:42,780 --> 00:05:43,780
How's my writing?

105
00:05:43,870 --> 00:05:44,670
Am I rusty now?

106
00:05:46,040 --> 00:05:46,750
Over these past few years,

107
00:05:46,750 --> 00:05:48,210
judgements are all I've been writing.

108
00:05:48,210 --> 00:05:49,920
Tell me what you think

109
00:05:49,950 --> 00:05:50,590
of my work.

110
00:05:51,920 --> 00:05:53,520
Hey, what do you mean by this?

111
00:05:55,360 --> 00:05:56,690
What are you getting at?

112
00:05:56,830 --> 00:05:57,830
A serious incident happened.

113
00:05:57,830 --> 00:05:59,760
I'm the one getting the credit now?

114
00:06:02,160 --> 00:06:03,800
Yes, and no, in a sense.

115
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:06,070
Now, the court needs to set up

116
00:06:06,070 --> 00:06:07,130
a positive example

117
00:06:07,620 --> 00:06:08,200
to tell everyone

118
00:06:08,200 --> 00:06:09,310
that in the Intermediate Court,

119
00:06:09,310 --> 00:06:10,190
besides judges like Mei Fang

120
00:06:10,190 --> 00:06:11,630
who are eager for quick success,

121
00:06:11,630 --> 00:06:13,180
there are still judges
like you, Xia Yingjie,

122
00:06:13,180 --> 00:06:14,840
who strictly uphold justice.

123
00:06:15,020 --> 00:06:15,680
Mei Fang and I were

124
00:06:15,680 --> 00:06:17,160
on a collegial panel.

125
00:06:17,720 --> 00:06:18,450
At that time,

126
00:06:18,560 --> 00:06:20,410
I didn't stick to my opinion till the end.

127
00:06:20,410 --> 00:06:22,010
I chose to make a concession.

128
00:06:22,160 --> 00:06:23,000
So I should bear

129
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:24,660
the responsibility with her.

130
00:06:24,720 --> 00:06:25,800
W-What's the point

131
00:06:25,830 --> 00:06:26,530
of writing this?

132
00:06:26,530 --> 00:06:27,510
Can you stop being

133
00:06:27,510 --> 00:06:28,970
so emotionally involved?

134
00:06:31,750 --> 00:06:32,630
If you take my advice,

135
00:06:32,630 --> 00:06:33,750
you can completely extricate yourself

136
00:06:33,750 --> 00:06:34,750
from this matter,

137
00:06:35,270 --> 00:06:36,560
and receive far more commendation

138
00:06:36,560 --> 00:06:37,890
than you could imagine.

139
00:06:40,070 --> 00:06:41,870
Thank you for looking out for me.

140
00:06:50,600 --> 00:06:52,130
Do you remember we teamed up

141
00:06:52,310 --> 00:06:53,170
for a moot court

142
00:06:53,970 --> 00:06:54,890
competition

143
00:06:54,920 --> 00:06:56,180
in our sophomore year?

144
00:06:56,510 --> 00:06:57,159
I remember.

145
00:06:57,159 --> 00:06:59,360
We lost to Yizhong and got second place.

146
00:06:59,700 --> 00:07:02,160
It was our first time
getting a certificate.

147
00:07:02,430 --> 00:07:05,120
We both got drunk
on the day of the award ceremony.

148
00:07:05,120 --> 00:07:07,050
I couldn't believe I worked so hard

149
00:07:08,190 --> 00:07:09,590
only to get second place.

150
00:07:10,920 --> 00:07:12,850
While drinking, I cried and puked.

151
00:07:13,630 --> 00:07:15,430
It was you who stayed up all night

152
00:07:16,230 --> 00:07:17,270
to draw a first-prize certificate

153
00:07:17,270 --> 00:07:18,160
for me.

154
00:07:20,160 --> 00:07:22,290
Even the official seal looked so real.

155
00:07:24,480 --> 00:07:26,080
At that time, I made up my mind

156
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:29,400
that in the future, I must

157
00:07:30,050 --> 00:07:31,280
win a genuine

158
00:07:31,310 --> 00:07:32,040
first prize.

159
00:07:32,070 --> 00:07:34,870
That's why you truly deserve
the credit this time.

160
00:07:36,480 --> 00:07:36,870
No.

161
00:07:39,040 --> 00:07:40,700
This time is just like before.

162
00:07:41,480 --> 00:07:43,940
You've drawn me another prize certificate.

163
00:07:45,500 --> 00:07:46,560
This is also a fake.

164
00:07:58,640 --> 00:07:59,870
You are too hard on yourself,

165
00:07:59,870 --> 00:08:00,600
Xia Yingjie.

166
00:08:02,430 --> 00:08:04,360
Chief Judge Yu, please believe me.

167
00:08:05,160 --> 00:08:07,490
I'm not afraid of being held accountable.

168
00:08:07,950 --> 00:08:09,160
I'm ready to be punished

169
00:08:09,160 --> 00:08:10,490
for my past indecision.

170
00:08:10,720 --> 00:08:11,800
Also, I implore you

171
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:14,860
to allow me to win fair and square.

172
00:08:15,270 --> 00:08:15,800
Okay?

173
00:08:44,480 --> 00:08:45,080
Xia,

174
00:08:45,960 --> 00:08:47,080
Chief Judge Yu

175
00:08:47,790 --> 00:08:49,190
told us to write a report.

176
00:08:49,550 --> 00:08:52,030
Should I write it or you?

177
00:08:52,480 --> 00:08:53,610
You should write it.

178
00:08:54,870 --> 00:08:56,070
Is it appropriate...

179
00:08:56,390 --> 00:08:57,390
for me to write it?

180
00:08:59,360 --> 00:09:01,560
You were the presiding judge back then.

181
00:09:02,440 --> 00:09:04,170
That's exactly why I hesitate.

182
00:09:04,240 --> 00:09:05,630
I'm worried that if I write it,

183
00:09:05,630 --> 00:09:08,230
they'll say I'm glossing over
the real issues.

184
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:10,400
You should do it instead.

185
00:09:11,960 --> 00:09:13,360
Fine, I'll write it then.

186
00:09:14,930 --> 00:09:16,170
But you must not admit

187
00:09:16,200 --> 00:09:17,400
that it was our fault.

188
00:09:17,600 --> 00:09:18,730
In fact, it was never

189
00:09:18,740 --> 00:09:19,690
our fault.

190
00:09:19,910 --> 00:09:21,390
Whether to sentence him
to death or death with reprieve

191
00:09:21,390 --> 00:09:23,080
was decided by the higher-ups.

192
00:09:23,080 --> 00:09:25,010
It really had nothing to do with us.

193
00:09:26,390 --> 00:09:26,910
Mei,

194
00:09:27,910 --> 00:09:29,040
if I'm writing this,

195
00:09:29,750 --> 00:09:31,350
I won't try to defend myself.

196
00:09:31,670 --> 00:09:33,270
I'll accept any punishment.

197
00:09:35,560 --> 00:09:36,120
Wait, Xia Yingjie.

198
00:09:36,120 --> 00:09:37,360
What do you mean by that?

199
00:09:37,360 --> 00:09:38,270
So you get to play the saint,

200
00:09:38,270 --> 00:09:39,730
while I take the fall, huh?

201
00:09:40,240 --> 00:09:41,750
You'll accept any punishment?

202
00:09:41,750 --> 00:09:43,210
I was the presiding judge.

203
00:09:43,310 --> 00:09:44,550
Will you be the one to get punished?

204
00:09:44,550 --> 00:09:45,030
If there's punishment,

205
00:09:45,030 --> 00:09:46,270
I'll be the first one to take it!

206
00:09:46,270 --> 00:09:46,790
Mei,

207
00:09:47,600 --> 00:09:48,660
don't get it wrong.

208
00:09:49,510 --> 00:09:51,110
We were on a collegial panel.

209
00:09:51,520 --> 00:09:52,630
The two of us delivered the verdict

210
00:09:52,630 --> 00:09:53,720
of the case together.

211
00:09:53,720 --> 00:09:54,980
If there's liability,

212
00:09:55,120 --> 00:09:55,920
it'll be ours.

213
00:09:57,720 --> 00:09:59,580
I swear to share the woes with you.

214
00:10:08,960 --> 00:10:09,820
Tian Mingyuan.

215
00:10:09,910 --> 00:10:10,240
Here.

216
00:10:11,550 --> 00:10:12,280
Ren Xiaojun.

217
00:10:13,120 --> 00:10:13,510
Here.

218
00:10:16,480 --> 00:10:17,080
Yan Jicai.

219
00:10:18,080 --> 00:10:18,440
Here!

220
00:10:27,120 --> 00:10:27,650
Jin Jian.

221
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:28,360
Here.

222
00:10:29,320 --> 00:10:30,050
Hao Xuefeng.

223
00:10:30,390 --> 00:10:30,790
Here!

224
00:10:32,630 --> 00:10:33,230
Wu Lidong.

225
00:10:33,390 --> 00:10:33,720
Here.

226
00:10:34,390 --> 00:10:35,030
Yi Dayong.

227
00:10:35,790 --> 00:10:36,200
Here!

228
00:10:37,910 --> 00:10:39,630
Human tissue was found

229
00:10:39,630 --> 00:10:41,510
under 8 of the victim's fingernails.

230
00:10:41,510 --> 00:10:43,510
It proves that the victim struggled

231
00:10:43,630 --> 00:10:45,360
with someone before her death.

232
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:47,240
Does the DNA match

233
00:10:47,600 --> 00:10:49,030
Yan Jicai's?

234
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:50,860
No, it doesn't.

235
00:10:52,440 --> 00:10:53,870
What does the file say?

236
00:10:54,490 --> 00:10:55,330
The file says

237
00:10:55,360 --> 00:10:56,360
such human tissue

238
00:10:56,390 --> 00:10:57,920
is not relevant to the case.

239
00:11:00,360 --> 00:11:02,090
Yan Jicai's counsel mentioned

240
00:11:02,160 --> 00:11:03,030
that it was not until the fourth day

241
00:11:03,030 --> 00:11:04,510
after the incident that Yan was arrested.

242
00:11:04,510 --> 00:11:05,870
No injuries were found on his body

243
00:11:05,870 --> 00:11:07,800
during the physical examination,

244
00:11:07,870 --> 00:11:09,330
not even a single scratch.

245
00:11:10,840 --> 00:11:11,750
Did the victim not resist

246
00:11:11,750 --> 00:11:12,680
before she died?

247
00:11:12,960 --> 00:11:13,750
If not,

248
00:11:14,240 --> 00:11:15,670
why were there skin flakes

249
00:11:15,670 --> 00:11:16,600
under her nails?

250
00:11:17,260 --> 00:11:17,960
And such human tissue

251
00:11:17,960 --> 00:11:19,560
doesn't belong to Yan Jicai.

252
00:11:20,840 --> 00:11:21,870
Listen to this...

253
00:11:23,600 --> 00:11:24,670
Mentor, won't you say

254
00:11:24,670 --> 00:11:26,000
it's a logical paradox?

255
00:11:28,050 --> 00:11:28,690
How did

256
00:11:28,720 --> 00:11:29,980
the police explain it?

257
00:11:30,430 --> 00:11:31,210
They believed

258
00:11:31,210 --> 00:11:33,120
that Yan Jicai launched a sudden attack.

259
00:11:33,120 --> 00:11:34,780
The girl was caught off guard.

260
00:11:35,390 --> 00:11:37,720
Losing the ability to resist in an instant

261
00:11:38,030 --> 00:11:38,960
often causes

262
00:11:38,980 --> 00:11:40,210
obvious or severe

263
00:11:40,240 --> 00:11:41,370
physical injuries.

264
00:11:41,790 --> 00:11:44,050
Unless the killer is a real professional

265
00:11:44,280 --> 00:11:45,550
who knows human anatomy

266
00:11:45,550 --> 00:11:47,210
and masters certain methods.

267
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:51,260
Does Yan Jicai have that kind of ability?

268
00:11:51,270 --> 00:11:52,390
The autopsy report says

269
00:11:52,390 --> 00:11:54,140
the girl was strangled to death.

270
00:11:54,140 --> 00:11:55,290
There are no signs

271
00:11:55,320 --> 00:11:56,850
of severe blows to her head.

272
00:11:57,360 --> 00:11:58,030
What else?

273
00:11:58,840 --> 00:11:59,390
The time.

274
00:12:00,460 --> 00:12:01,840
Yan Jicai couldn't have possibly done

275
00:12:01,840 --> 00:12:04,440
the crime at the time
stated in his confession.

276
00:12:04,510 --> 00:12:06,150
This can be deduced from the time shown

277
00:12:06,150 --> 00:12:07,680
on the surveillance video.

278
00:12:09,380 --> 00:12:11,720
For such a heinous rape and murder case,

279
00:12:11,750 --> 00:12:14,670
the court only gave Yan
a death sentence with reprieve.

280
00:12:14,670 --> 00:12:16,390
That's a message itself.

281
00:12:18,750 --> 00:12:21,270
A judgment that leaves room for doubt.

282
00:12:21,910 --> 00:12:22,360
Yes.

283
00:12:24,200 --> 00:12:24,910
Just another

284
00:12:24,910 --> 00:12:26,970
judgment that leaves room for doubt.

285
00:12:29,080 --> 00:12:30,150
Mentor, I think...

286
00:12:30,440 --> 00:12:31,750
Yan Jicai might really have been

287
00:12:31,750 --> 00:12:33,080
wrongfully convicted.

288
00:12:33,630 --> 00:12:34,960
Wrongfully convicted?

289
00:12:35,750 --> 00:12:37,680
Then tell me who the real killer is.

290
00:12:45,840 --> 00:12:47,540
[Details revealed about the necrophilic
murder by Jia Peng the taxi driver]

291
00:12:46,260 --> 00:12:47,720
